Third-party content and models
------------------------------

Playa Angel model weights (downloaded by the app, not part of this
repository) are published at
https://huggingface.co/davidryalpug/playa-angel. The three tiers do
not share one base model, so the license attaches PER FILE, not to
"the weights" as a group. src/llm/modelCatalog.ts pins the exact file
each tier downloads.

Playa Angel Max (angel-max.gguf, built from angel-v44g-e4b-q4_0.gguf)
is a fine-tuned, quantized derivative of Google's Gemma 4 E4B. It is a
Model Derivative under the Gemma Terms of Use
(https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms) and is distributed subject to
them. Those terms carry use restrictions (section 3.2, which
incorporates the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy at
https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy), and those
restrictions apply to anyone who uses or redistributes this file. The
base weights were modified by fine-tuning and by quantization. A copy
of the Gemma Terms of Use ships with the weights.

  Gemma is provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms of Use found at ai.google.dev/gemma/terms

Google claims no rights in the text a Gemma model generates (section
3.3). The Gemma terms grant no rights in Google's trademarks (section
4.2), and this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.

Playa Angel and Playa Angel Light (angel-smart.gguf and
angel-light.gguf) are one fine-tuned derivative of LFM2.5 by Liquid AI
(https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI) at two quantizations, distributed
under the LFM Open License v1.0. That license conditions commercial
use on an annual revenue threshold (see the license text shipped with
the weights); the same condition applies to any use of the derivative
weights.

The two schemes do not conflict, because they attach to different
files. Neither one covers all three tiers, and no single license
covers "Playa Angel" as a whole.

The bundled survival-guide pack summarizes and, where marked, quotes
preparedness and cultural material from Burning Man Project
(https://burningman.org), including the Ten Principles, with source
attribution in the pack headings. Provenance: authored 2026-08 from
burningman.org survival/preparedness pages and the published 2026 event
dates; transformation = curated summaries plus marked verbatim passages;
the built pack ships as assets/packs/survival-guide/guide.md.json. Burning Man, Black Rock City, and
related marks belong to Burning Man Project. This project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Burning Man Project.

Event listings are built from Burning Man's public playa events data
(playaevents.burningman.org), fetched 2026-08 by tools/fetch_playaevents.py
(cached, rate-limited crawl); transformation = parsing to structured rows,
no editorial changes, plus seven hand-authored city-milestone rows
(gates open, Man burn, Temple burn, exodus — tools/data/
brc-2026-city-milestones.jsonl) sourced from the published 2026
schedule. Placement addresses join at the pre-event data drop.

Veteran technique summaries are curated from Burn.Life
(https://burn.life) with per-article credit and links, summarized
rather than reproduced.

The YouTube lore tooling fetches transcripts for PERSONAL, LOCAL use
only; no transcript content is included in or distributed with this
repository.
